# ESP biometric protocol

TCP server on **port 9000** (`espSocket.ts`). One line per message, fields separated by `:`.

| Command | Request | Success reply |
|---------|---------|---------------|
| Lookup | `LOOKUP:<id>` | `LOOKUP:<id>:SET` or `LOOKUP:<id>:GET` |
| Enroll | `SET:<id>:<gaps>` | `SET:<id>:OK` |
| Verify | `GET:<id>:<gaps>` | `GET:<id>:1` or `GET:<id>:0` |
| Error | — | `ERROR:<CODE>` (e.g. `NOT_FOUND`) |

## Pattern format

- Gaps in ms: `"320,890,410"` (≥3 gaps; typical 4 gaps ⇒ 5 knocks).
- Match via `patternsMatch()` — mean-normalized ratios, `REL_TOLERANCE ≈ 0.38`.
- Do not hash patterns; store raw gap string on `User.biometricPattern`.
- MCU enroll: capture primary + confirm locally, upload `SET` only on match.

## Host duties

- Parse in `espSocket.ts`; business logic in `biometric.ts`.
- Broadcast `esp:status` / `esp:log` and `activity:new` to renderer.
- Never invent HTTP/JSON endpoints for ESP — TCP colon text only.
